title The room a name never said
prompt Continuation of the same lap -- the cold endurance run reddened tool_letter_room at guard 57 after the door work had landed, and reds outrank lane tidiness.
think The red named three bearing_quorum files sitting in the m room when the letter rule computes b from their basenames. I checked the claim board first: four peer claims live, none naming those paths, and the lap that landed them at e5e6f1729 had already shelved its account.
think git mv carried all three modes intact -- 100644 for the witness, 100755 for the two fixtures -- which is the exec-bit law's own reason for preferring it to a copy.
think Then the whole-tree sweep for inbound references, because references are promises. Twelve files named the old paths; six were living and six carried dated basenames, so six were repointed in place through the original inode and six kept every word they wrote.
think The repoint reddened whitepaper_definitions at 35 of 55 legs, and the shape of the failure was the interesting part: every failed leg read wanted=changed got=unchanged, which reads as a mutation that stopped biting rather than a pen that was never built.
think The cause was one line. whitepaper_definitions_control.sh names the room alone on its mkdir -p -- $_d/tools/fixtures/m -- and then writes its stub into the repointed file path. My sed matched <room>/<file> and could never match a directory named without a file, so the pen wrote into a directory that no longer existed and the write failed in silence.
think I proved the red was mine rather than pre-existing by stashing the whole move and running the witness at committed HEAD, where it read control_failed=0. A red inherited and a red caused want two different repairs.
obs The guard that caught the directory blindness was the one downstream of the move, rather than the one doing it. A sweep keyed on a path finds paths; a pen builds a room, and those are two different nouns in the same string.
obs tool_letter_room reads the INDEX rather than the working tree, so a completed move left unstaged still reds -- which it did once mid-repair, after a stash cycle broke the renames into unstaged deletions. Staging them brought entries 3330 back to 3327 and misfiled to 0.
obs No file was deleted and no reference was left dangling: six living citers repointed, six dated citers left as testimony, and the moved witness GREEN on metal at its new path.
rota lap 5002, row 2 -- Fire, the row that sees. Already recorded in this lap's first log; the threshold's line that the lap which squints cuts twice read directly onto this repair, since the first sweep was the squint and reading the failed legs one at a time was the look.
loom red=749 guard=tool_letter_room misfiled_before=3 misfiled_after=0 entries=3327 files_moved=3 citers_living=6 citers_dated=6
